<title>NEW ZEALAND: Power NZ boosts half-year net profit by 20.6 pct. [CORRECTED 03:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Power NZ boosts half-year net profit by 20.6 pct. [CORRECTED 03:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline, deleting reference to full year)</p>
<p>Half year to Sept 30.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 27.83 vs 23.08</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 18.4 vs 15.2</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 11.0 vs 9.2</p>
<p>    Turnover				   182.5 vs 156.4</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			     40.6 vs 32.1</p>
<p>    Tax					   13.4 vs 10.4</p>
<p>    Equity earnings			   1.65 vs 1.38</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 151.5 vs same</p>
<p>    Dividend carries 5.42 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>    Pay date Dec 13</p>
<p>    Reg date Dec 6</p>
<p>    Ex div   Dec 12</p>
<p>    Note - Power New Zealand Ltd is an Auckland-based electricity distributor.</p>
<p>    -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746 (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
</text>
